sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To find the sixth apotome.
----
proof:

Set out a rational straight line {A}, and set out three numbers {E}, {BC}, and {CD} not having to one another the ratio which a square number has to a square number, and further let {CB} also not have to {BD} the ratio which a square number has to a square number.

Let it be contrived that {E} is to {BC} as the square on {A} is to the square on {FG}, and {BC} is to {CD} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH}. [!just X.6.Cor]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="240" height="195" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.90 diagram" src="propX90.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the rational line A, the apotome FH (H on FG), the
    // line K whose square is the excess of the square on FG over the square
    // on GH, the number E (blue), and the number BC (blue) with D on it.
    // Added, all hidden at rest: transparent targets CD, BD (;0;0;0) for the
    // numbers, GH (;0;0;0) for the part cut from FG, and FH (;0;0;0) for the
    // apotome. FG already strokes from F, so it needs no twin. The walk is
    // highlight beats plus the strokes of A, FG and K as the text sets them
    // out.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A1, A2 (the line A) and the
    // offscreen frees; E1, E2, B, C, D, F and K1 are line sliders the proof
    // only reaches later, so they are deferred. G, H and K2 are derived and
    // listed per slide.
