            { text: "Again, since {BC} is to {CD} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH},",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["BC","CD","FG","GH"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {FG} is commensurable with the square on {GH}.",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.6" }] },
            { text: "But the square on {FG} is rational, therefore the square on {GH} is also rational.",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"] },
            { text: "Therefore {GH} is also rational.",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["GH"] },
            { text: "Since {BC} does not have to {CD} the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["BC","CD"] },
            { text: "therefore neither does the square on {FG} have to the square on {GH}",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"] },
            { text: "the ratio which a square number has to a square number.",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"] },
            { text: "Therefore {FG} is incommensurable in length with {GH}",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FG, GH incommensurable in length", ref: "X.9" }] },
            { text: "And both are rational, therefore {FG} and {GH} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only.",
              visible: TGH,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"] },
            { text: "Therefore {FH} is an apotome.",
              visible: APO,
              highlighted: ["FH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FH apotome", ref: "X.73" }] },
            { text: "I say next that it is also a sixth apotome.",
              visible: APO,
              highlighted: ["FH"] },
            { text: "Since {E} is to {BC} as the square on {A} is to the square on {FG},",
              visible: APO,
              highlighted: ["E","BC","A","FG"] },
            { text: "and {BC} is to {CD} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH},",
              visible: APO,
              highlighted: ["BC","CD","FG","GH"] },
            { text: "therefore, ex aequali, {E} is to {CD} as the square on {A} is to the square on {GH}.",
              visible: APO,
              highlighted: ["E","CD","A","GH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "E : CD = A² : GH²", ref: "V.22" }] },
            { text: "But {E} does not have to {CD} the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: APO,
              highlighted: ["E","CD"] },
            { text: "therefore neither does the square on {A} have to the square on {GH}",
              visible: APO,
              highlighted: ["A","GH"] },
            { text: "the ratio which a square number has to a square number.",
              visible: APO,
              highlighted: ["A","GH"] },
            { text: "Therefore {A} is incommensurable in length with {GH}.",
              visible: APO,
              highlighted: ["A","GH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "A, GH incommensurable in length", ref: "X.9" }] },
            { text: "Therefore neither of the straight lines {FG} nor {GH} is commensurable in length with the rational straight line {A}.",
              visible: APO,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH","A"] },
            { text: "Now let the square on {K} be that by which the square on {FG} is greater than the square on {GH}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["K","FG","GH"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "K", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Since {BC} is to {CD} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","CD","FG","GH"] },
            { text: "therefore, in conversion, {CB} is to {BD} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {K}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","BD","FG","K"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CB : BD = FG² : K²", ref: "V.19.Cor" }] },
            { text: "But {CB} does not have to {BD} the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","BD"] },
            { text: "therefore neither does the square on {FG} have to the square on {K}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","K"] },
            { text: "the ratio which a square number has to a square number,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","K"] },
            { text: "therefore {FG} is incommensurable in length with {K}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","K"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FG, K incommensurable in length", ref: "X.9" }] },
            { text: "And the square on {FG} is greater than the square on {GH} by the square on {K},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH","K"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {FG} is greater than the square on {GH}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line incommensurable in length with {FG}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["K","FG"] },
            { text: "And neither of the straight lines {FG} nor {GH} is commensurable with the rational straight line {A} set out.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FG","GH","A"] },
            { text: "Therefore {FH} is a sixth apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FH"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.Def.III.6" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the sixth apotome {FH} has been found.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FH"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.90") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "V.19.Cor":    "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV19/#cor",
        "V.22":        "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV22/",
        "X.6":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX6/",
        "X.6.Cor":     "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX6/#cor",
        "X.9":         "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX9/",
        "X.73":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX73/",
        "X.Def.III.6": "/elements/books/bookX/definitions/defX.III.6/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Now since {E} is to {BC} as the square on {A} is to the square on {FG}, therefore the square on {A} is commensurable with the square on {FG}. [!just X.6]

But the square on {A} is rational, therefore the square on {FG} is also rational. Therefore {FG} is also rational.

Since {E} does not have to {BC} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore neither does the square on {A} have to the square on {FG} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore {A} is incommensurable in length with {FG}. [!just X.9]

Again, since {BC} is to {CD} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH}, therefore the square on {FG} is commensurable with the square on {GH}. [!just X.6]

But the square on {FG} is rational, therefore the square on {GH} is also rational. Therefore {GH} is also rational.

Since {BC} does not have to {CD} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore neither does the square on {FG} have to the square on {GH} the ratio which a square number has to a square number. Therefore {FG} is incommensurable in length with {GH} [!just X.9]

And both are rational, therefore {FG} and {GH} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. Therefore {FH} is an apotome. [!just X.73]

I say next that it is also a sixth apotome.

Since {E} is to {BC} as the square on {A} is to the square on {FG}, and {BC} is to {CD} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH}, therefore, *ex aequali*, {E} is to {CD} as the square on {A} is to the square on {GH}. [!just V.22]

But {E} does not have to {CD} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore neither does the square on {A} have to the square on {GH} the ratio which a square number has to a square number. Therefore {A} is incommensurable in length with {GH}. Therefore neither of the straight lines {FG} nor {GH} is commensurable in length with the rational straight line {A}. [!just X.9]

Now let the square on {K} be that by which the square on {FG} is greater than the square on {GH}.

Since {BC} is to {CD} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {GH}, therefore, in conversion, {CB} is to {BD} as the square on {FG} is to the square on {K}. [!just V.19.Cor]

But {CB} does not have to {BD} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore neither does the square on {FG} have to the square on {K} the ratio which a square number has to a square number, therefore {FG} is incommensurable in length with {K}. [!just X.9]

And the square on {FG} is greater than the square on {GH} by the square on {K}, therefore the square on {FG} is greater than the square on {GH} by the square on a straight line incommensurable in length with {FG}.

And neither of the straight lines {FG} nor {GH} is commensurable with the rational straight line {A} set out. Therefore {FH} is a sixth apotome. [!just X.Def.III.6]

Therefore the sixth apotome {FH} has been found.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
